{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008163-making-discplines-more-useful-in-combat","id":1008163,"title":"Making discplines more useful in combat?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-25T10:12:17-08:00","id":1008163,"title":"Making discplines more useful in combat?","content":"I was reading White Wolf wiki and came across <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Differences_between_Vampire:_The_Masquerade_and_Vampire:_The_Requiem\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Disciplines have broadly changed to make them less helpful in combat and more helpful in other ways. A number of original clans (some now <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Bloodline\" target=\"_blank\">bloodlines</a>) have changed in theme and gained different <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Discipline\" target=\"_blank\">Disciplines</a> to reflect this; for example, the <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Nosferatu\" target=\"_blank\">Nosferatu</a> have changed from revolting outcasts to actual monsters, and the entirely new <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Nightmare\" target=\"_blank\">Nightmare</a> Discipline helps them maintain this image. </div> </div> </div>I guess this is one of the few things that I'm concerned or critical about in Requiem that your disciplines are less helpful in combat therefore making your character weaker compared to the average VtM vampire although is 2nd edition different though?<br /> <br /> Well this is one of the few things I've liked in Masquerade was the fact that disciplines were not only powerful but also sufficient in combat making you quite formidable and easily translated into a video game while I heard in Requiem it's watered down to the point I remember reading in one review that it almost makes your character like a mortal or am I wrong?<br /> <br /> Well honestly, just how powerful Requiem's disciplines are and can they hold a candle to Masquerade's? Is it even possible to beef them up to make them not only combat sufficient but also just port the Masquerade disciplines into Requiem with no changes? Especially those who are playing combat heavy and powerhouse games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 11-25-2016, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T10:53:48-08:00","id":1008195,"title":"","content":"Always be wary of making secondhand mechanical judgments. It's like a game of telephone: slight distortions build up as ideas pass from listener to listener.<br /> <br /> You're not going to have luck trying to run Masquerade Discipline rules in a Requiem game. Not only are certain mechanics, like extra actions/attacks in one turn, seriously unbalanced for the CofD system in general, but the dice rolling mechanic itself is different in ways that will confuse and mess it up.<br /> <br /> Requiem Disciplines are absolutely sufficient for use in combat. First edition Vampire: The Requiem does have less of a gulf of threat between the living and the dead, and if you're the type to run crossover with other gamelines, Requiem was sometimes considered to have been left behind in capabilities compared to characters from later gamelines, although Requiem characters also had some of the lowest-investment access to inflicting aggravated damage, which became pretty rare in later gamelines. Second edition Requiem beefs vampires up significantly in hardiness. It also ratchets down that outlier access to aggravated damage, but it wasn't really needed; aggravated damage doesn't have the presence in CofD games that it does in WoD.<br /> <br /> Basically: a Requiem vampire has a definite (1e) or overwhelming (2e) advantage over a mortal human. They're just not generally going to cuisinart them in one round. And, like in WoD, probably the nastiest things you can do to a human involve never letting them get into a fight with you in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T11:05:09-08:00","id":1008203,"title":"","content":"Yeah, if you read Requiem 2E, you're not going to be disappointed with combat utility, re: disciplines. Animalism 5 basically lets you weaponize your domain, and Nightmare can scare people so badly they take lethal damage (which is hard to do to Kindred in Requiem). As SL says, the wiki description is a little out of date here, and it's second hand information anyway. As I said in the other thread, the objection isn't that some of the facets of old powers could kill really well, it's that that was all some of them could do, even when that didn't make sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T11:42:13-08:00","id":1008225,"title":"","content":"The power curve is a little flatter in 2e Requiem than in V20 Masquerade. A starting vampire in Requiem is considerably more threatening than a starting vampire in Masquerade, and it's easier to accumulate power, including combat power, faster. The flip side is that Masquerade vampires have a higher ceiling. An elder in Requiem is a terrifying monster, but it doesn't hold a candle to the blood gods that Masquerade's Methuselah could become with enough experience.<br /> <br /> As for combat ability, Requiem vampires have it. The physical Disciplines - Celerity, Vigor (the Potence analogue), and Resilience (the Fortitude analogue) are incredible without breaking CofD's combat system. The more cerebral Disciplines also have their combat applications, though it's true that some of their most potent and frightening abilities involve screwing you over long before combat ever starts. Physical Intensity means even a vampire with no combat investment can still overwhelm most mortal opponents if they're willing to spend enough Vitae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T12:25:05-08:00","id":1008236,"title":"","content":"Experience spent directly towards becoming a combat specialist will make you combat specialist better, faster and stronger than spending these XP towards Disciplines (well, with some exceptions - but those tend to synergize with combat purchases, instead of just being flat better). This is a good thing, because XP spent towards becoming a combat threat should make you a combat threat. This doesn't mean, at the same time, that Disciplines can't contribute towards your victory. In fact, while they might not interact with your combat stats directly, they might give you alternate methods of combat resolution that don't rely on standard methods. <br /> <br /> Remember, in 2nd ED, combat is goal oriented - and you should evaluate options with that in mind. Does it help progress towards that goal faster? Or, maybe, it gives you a whole new way of solving the encounter? Disciplines tends to provide you with both of these.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T13:38:23-08:00","id":1008254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008163-making-discplines-more-useful-in-combat?p=1008225#post1008225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The flip side is that Masquerade vampires have a higher ceiling. An elder in Requiem is a terrifying monster, but it doesn't hold a candle to the blood gods that Masquerade's Methuselah could become with enough experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's where the main issue lies since Vampires in Requiem can't get as powerful as a Masquerade Methuselah hence they can't become 'blood gods' (although as long it's not in world destroying proportions like the Antediluvians though).<br /> <br /> Although I just now thinking of a idea of a &quot;Blood Potency and Generation&quot; mixture that if a Vampire has lower generation then their blood potency allows them to do more powerful feats while vampires of higher generations their BP exhausts more quickly if they use too much power that their generation can support. What I mean is that lower generations can hold so much power due to their blood potency being longer than 10 while higher generation vampires go into 'exhaustion' after increasing their power around 10 or after.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 11-25-2016, 04:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T13:42:17-08:00","id":1008255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008163-making-discplines-more-useful-in-combat#post1008163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I heard in Requiem it's watered down to the point I remember reading in one review that it almost makes your character like a mortal or am I wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can <i>easily</i> build a starting vampire capable of throwing a small car. So no, they don't feel particularly like a mortal.<br /> <br /> And to be honest I think saying requiem vamps can't get as powerful as masquerade Methuselahs is a bit premature. The fact is we don't <i>know</i> what they can really do. Some of the elder-tier devotions are pretty crazy. (become totally invulnerable,. turn into an amorphous shapeshifting blob of teeth, claws and death, <i>summon an actual biblical plague of vermin) </i>So who knows what they can do if they really put their mind to it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 11-25-2016, 04:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T13:57:37-08:00","id":1008260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008163-making-discplines-more-useful-in-combat?p=1008255#post1008255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can <i>easily</i> build a starting vampire capable of throwing a small car. So no, they don't feel particularly like a mortal.<br /> <br /> And to be honest I think saying requiem vamps can't get as powerful as masquerade Methuselahs is a bit premature. The fact is we don't <i>know</i> what they can really do. Some of the elder-tier devotions are pretty crazy. (become totally invulnerable,. turn into an amorphous shapeshifting blob of teeth, claws and death, <i>summon an actual biblical plague of vermin) </i>So who knows what they can do if they really put their mind to it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess it means they're capable summoning shadow tentacles and throwing cars around and ripping adversaries apart with them? Well if Requiem's Obtenebration can do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T14:02:03-08:00","id":1008261,"title":"","content":"Have you tried Beast gameline?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T14:08:04-08:00","id":1008264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008163-making-discplines-more-useful-in-combat?p=1008260#post1008260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess it means they're capable summoning shadow tentacles and throwing cars around and ripping adversaries apart with them? Well if Requiem's Obtenebration can do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Obtenebration can't really do that, but a BP10 elder? Yeah, sure. Probably involve Protean and Nightmare or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T14:09:44-08:00","id":1008265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008163-making-discplines-more-useful-in-combat?p=1008255#post1008255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And to be honest I think saying requiem vamps can't get as powerful as masquerade Methuselahs is a bit premature. The fact is we don't <i>know</i> what they can really do. Some of the elder-tier devotions are pretty crazy. (become totally invulnerable,. turn into an amorphous shapeshifting blob of teeth, claws and death, <i>summon an actual biblical plague of vermin) </i>So who knows what they can do if they really put their mind to it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I did mean within the limits of currently available options. I expect Thousand Years of Night will eventually bring us even more incredible elder Devotions and wouldn't be surprised to see other ways to expand an elder's power. I doubt Antediluvian level &quot;plot device&quot; powers, but I would bet money we'll see the power ceiling raised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T14:10:36-08:00","id":1008266,"title":"","content":"I would not be surprised if that review was for VtR 1E where starting vampires were extremely squishy. 2E has definitely upped the power levels for even starting vampires. And while the extremely powerful vampires in VtR might not have the same supernatural powers as in VtM, they are most definitely gods when it comes to physical prowess.<br /> With nothing more than official 2E rules and a huge pile of XP I can build a vampire who can throw that car with 102 dice. Or stab someone with 114 dice, 9-Again, Rote Action with a 7L weapon (that still deals Lethal to vampires). Of course, that's the extreme end of the scale and requires a huge Vitae expenditure, but even half of that dice pool would turn any mortal into chunky salsa.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh, and reduce those dice pools with 10 and the vampire can also reflexively become 100% impervious to any harm for the rest of the turn, including aggravated damage and damage from the great banes. You know, in case someone would want to attack that monstrosity after seeing what it did to your friend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 11-25-2016, 05:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T14:12:40-08:00","id":1008267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008163-making-discplines-more-useful-in-combat?p=1008260#post1008260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess it means they're capable summoning shadow tentacles and throwing cars around and ripping adversaries apart with them? Well if Requiem's Obtenebration can do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't Obtenebration originally written to be an antagonist power, and isn't it generally considered overpowered to the point of being inappropriate for most player characters in Masquerade? Conversely, Requiem 2e's Obten is powerful without breaking the CofD system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-25-2016, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T14:53:28-08:00","id":1008280,"title":"","content":"The antagonistic/protagonist split is discussed in thread next to this one, Translation of Masquerade Powers, I believe. It involves the same user, so you can basically read up their stance on that preemptively.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I suggested Beast because it's powers seem to fit the aesthetics of Shadow Tentacle Monster and similar builds more than current iteration of Vampire. This is not a judgemental statement (I don't have any particular opinion about Lasombra, not my cup of tea), but I think that Beast might have better array of powers that might interest you. <br /> <br /> As for power levels, it's important to remember that in comparison to Masquerade, lower ceiling went up but upper ceiling went lower. That is, as long as we are talking about prewritten powers; Requiem left a good design tool that can be used to adjust these higher power levels to your liking by introduction of...these special powers that you learn by spending extra XP and which have extra requirement, like knowledge of multiple disciplines. So if you want your Elders to go Full JoJo, you can adjust the power level directly by altering how powerful late-game perks are. Game is fairly modular, so as long as you do it consequently, it should remain stable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T14:54:53-08:00","id":1008281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008163-making-discplines-more-useful-in-combat?p=1008225#post1008225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The power curve is a little flatter in 2e Requiem than in V20 Masquerade. A starting vampire in Requiem is considerably more threatening than a starting vampire in Masquerade, and it's easier to accumulate power, including combat power, faster. The flip side is that Masquerade vampires have a higher ceiling. An elder in Requiem is a terrifying monster, but it doesn't hold a candle to the blood gods that Masquerade's Methuselah could become with enough experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I do not agree with this. I played Masquerade as well requiem 1ed and 2ed. I agree if we are talking about 1ed requiem discipline but definetely not if we are considering 2ed. <br /> I mean, a fifth power of requiem 2ed, often is at the same level of a level 6-7 of the comparative discipline of masquerade, and with devotion there are quite no limits. Take as example juggernaut gait that save you from a nuke bomb theoretically, or dark decree (I'm not sure about the name) that allow you to change the fate itself.<br /> <br /> About combat disciplines lets make a comparision between the physical ones:<br /> <br /> Vigor allow you to be more effective in hitting the targhet while Potence don't. Furthemore with Vigor you can emulate the power of potence dealing automatic damage.<br /> <br /> Resilence: definetely more powerful then Fortitutude; Reislence downgrade aggravated damage and allow you to negate resilence+1 lethal/bashing damages and, at the same time, resilence aggravated.<br /> <br /> Celerity, allow you to hit first, make surprise attack, and be more hard to hit. Here is hard to make a comparision because of the different basic system that don't allow you to do multiple actions. <br /> <br /> I definetly think that a requiem 2ed vampire with blood potency 7-8 is far more powerful than a mathuselah of masquerad in combat. Also because the frenzy and physical intensity sistem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 11-25-2016, 06:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T14:57:38-08:00","id":1008284,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Masquerade combat mechanics were a lot quirkier and clunkier, with combat powers being so strong mostly because they interacted with numbers in very...brutal way. Requiem powers are less number oriented and are more rooted in the core mechanics of the game itself, so all of the benefits aren't always immediately spottable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T15:08:25-08:00","id":1008285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008163-making-discplines-more-useful-in-combat?p=1008264#post1008264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Obtenebration can't really do that, but a BP10 elder? Yeah, sure. Probably involve Protean and Nightmare or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is, I actually want Obtenebration to do that at least that's how it was in Masquerade....<br /> <br /> I doubt Nightmare and Protean aren't going to capture that same aesthetic as Lasombra Obtenebration...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T15:15:50-08:00","id":1008287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008163-making-discplines-more-useful-in-combat?p=1008285#post1008285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thing is, I actually want Obtenebration to do that at least that's how it was in Masquerade....</div> </div> </div> </div>Despite the name, the proprietary Devotions of the Khabit Bloodline are simply not the unique Discipline of the Lasombra Clan.<br /> <br /> I don't think you will ever be satisfied with Requiem as long as you keep trying to compare it one-for-one with Masquerade like this. Vampire the Masquerade does a much better job of being Vampire the Masquerade than Vampire the Requiem does. If you want to play Vampire the Masquerade, I recommend playing Vampire the Masquerade. If you want to play Vampire the Requiem, I recommend discarding preconceptions based on your experience playing Masquerade and assessing it as its own, independent game (which it is).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-25-2016, 06:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T15:18:41-08:00","id":1008290,"title":"","content":"If you want Shadow Tentacles, I guess your best bet is to homebrew a Devotion. Pretty sure that people here could help you to express that aspect of the Discipline using Requiem's mechanical language.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T15:25:29-08:00","id":1008293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008163-making-discplines-more-useful-in-combat?p=1008287#post1008287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Despite the name, the proprietary Devotions of the Khabit Bloodline are simply not the unique Discipline of the Lasombra Clan.<br /> <br /> I don't think you will ever be satisfied with Requiem as long as you keep trying to compare it one-for-one with Masquerade like this. Vampire the Masquerade does a much better job of being Vampire the Masquerade than Vampire the Requiem does. If you want to play Vampire the Masquerade, I recommend playing Vampire the Masquerade. If you want to play Vampire the Requiem, I recommend discarding preconceptions based on your experience playing Masquerade and assessing it as its own, independent game (which it is).</div> </div> </div> </div>Although Masquerade has it's own problems like it's sects and it's clans shoehorning a certain mindset/philosophy not to mention how sects treat clans and mobility issues (for example, any Lasombra or Tzimisce outside the Sabbat are branded traitors by the former while the Camarilla and Anarchs would treat them as suspicion and hostility due to them being mistaken as Sabbat spies and being constantly on guard) which can make the game rather rigid and restrictive which one of the reasons why I turned to Requiem but even then I'm also running a few 'problems' such as what we're discussing now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 11-25-2016, 06:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T15:31:05-08:00","id":1008295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008163-making-discplines-more-useful-in-combat?p=1008293#post1008293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although Masquerade has it's own problems like it's sects and it's clans shoehorning a certain mindset/philosophy which can make the game rather rigid and restrictive which one of the reasons why I turned to Requiem but even then I'm also running a few 'problems' such as what we're discussing now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, indeed both games make design choices, some of which you may like and some of which you may dislike. That kind of comes with the territory of playing a game in a setting written and designed by someone else. Fortunately, the nature of RPGs means you are free to modify the setting and/or the mechanics to your liking in your own games.<br /> <br /> If what you want is to brew up a shadow tentacle power to use in Requiem, I recommend asking that, instead of asking how to change the Khabit Devotions into the Lasombra Discipline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T16:00:54-08:00","id":1008305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008163-making-discplines-more-useful-in-combat?p=1008267#post1008267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wasn't Obtenebration originally written to be an antagonist power, and isn't it generally considered overpowered to the point of being inappropriate for most player characters in Masquerade? Conversely, Requiem 2e's Obten is powerful without breaking the CofD system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. I'm not sure how this idea started, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/786915-13-licks-tricks-of-the-damned-vtm-disciplines-in-vtr?p=1008217#post1008217\">but it's not how things played out</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T16:07:01-08:00","id":1008309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008163-making-discplines-more-useful-in-combat?p=1008305#post1008305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. I'm not sure how this idea started, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/786915-13-licks-tricks-of-the-damned-vtm-disciplines-in-vtr?p=1008217#post1008217\">but it's not how things played out</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, cool, good to know. That's what I get for relying on second hand information about the game. Oh, the irony! XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T16:15:33-08:00","id":1008315,"title":"","content":"Y'know, there <i>is </i>something that can straight up do shadowy tentacles in the Requiem 2e book.<br /> <br /> It's Smoke and Mirrors, a Strix power. They need to buy it twice and be Shadow Potency 7 to do any damage with it though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T16:16:58-08:00","id":1008316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008163-making-discplines-more-useful-in-combat?p=1008315#post1008315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Y'know, there <i>is </i>something that can straight up do shadowy tentacles in the Requiem 2e book.<br /> <br /> It's Smoke and Mirrors, a Strix power. They need to buy it twice and be Shadow Potency 7 to do any damage with it though.</div> </div> </div> </div>But seems like only a Strix can use it (which are not only unplayable antagonists but also the vampires that actually are the empty husks that I was concerned about in earlier threads) however which is out of the question...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T16:36:13-08:00","id":1008320,"title":"","content":"Well, yeah, That's the point. It's not a common Kindred power because it's too Strix-like.<br /> <br /> But on the other hand, there's totally grounds to say that a Kindred saw the power and decided to try <i>imitating</i> it. Possibly to some funny looks from their peers. And some attempts at shining a light into their eyes to make sure they hadn't been possessed or anything. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T17:55:23-08:00","id":1008346,"title":"","content":"If nothing else, the Strix power provides some mechanical basis to work from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T14:05:05-08:00","id":1008676,"title":"","content":"Yeah, from what you're saying, it seems like you'd be better off playing the Masquerade mechanics with the Requiem background. If you like Requiem powers better, then, I'm thinking it'll be simpler using that system because you're going to have to do a lot of work transposing the disciplines for a close but still different system.<br /> <br /> Weeell, actually, you could also get this <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/86202/Vampire-Translation-Guide\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/...nslation-Guide</a><br /> Never actually tested it, but it seems like it could be helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T16:29:18-08:00","id":1012858,"title":"","content":"Oh one last question, does 2nd edition Requiem Vampires able to stand a chance against VtM vampires? If not then this is why their powers need a little more beefing up to match them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T16:39:11-08:00","id":1012863,"title":"","content":"You can use celerity 1 and vigor 4 to immediately stake someone with very little trouble right at the start of the confrontation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T16:48:38-08:00","id":1012869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008163-making-discplines-more-useful-in-combat?p=1012858#post1012858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh one last question, does 2nd edition Requiem Vampires able to stand a chance against VtM vampires? If not then this is why their powers need a little more beefing up to match them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well for one thing, the question is one of those &quot;could Batman beat up Spider-Man?&quot; things. They're from completely different fictional universes, so outside of non-canon crossover, there will never be a situation where they would be able to fight. On top of that, the games use different rule systems, so you would have to translate one into the other if you wanted to be able to test it from a purely meta-game perspective. Then, of course, you have to take context into account - in an empty white room where they're both naked, Spider-Man wins because without access to his gadgets, Batman is just a mundanely athletic guy who knows martial arts, whereas Spider-Man has super strength, reflexes, and limited precognition. But that situation would never actually happen, and if they both have access to their full suite of gadgets my money is on Batman. Unless you're in terrain where Spider-Man's wall crawling and webslinging can be used to his advantage. So, without proper context we can't give an answer with any kind of certainty.<br /> <br /> And even if it was found that the Masquerade vampire is the superior combattant in spite of all of the above considerations (which I actually highly doubt, Requiem vampires can be absolutely horrific combat wombats if they're built to be), why would that mean Requiem's Disciplines need to be beefed up to match them? They're different games with different goals, and the characters will never come into conflict with each other in actual play anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-05-2016, 07:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T20:00:51-08:00","id":1012945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008163-making-discplines-more-useful-in-combat?p=1012869#post1012869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And even if it was found that the Masquerade vampire is the superior combattant in spite of all of the above considerations (which I actually highly doubt, Requiem vampires can be absolutely horrific combat wombats if they're built to be), why would that mean Requiem's Disciplines need to be beefed up to match them? They're different games with different goals, and the characters will never come into conflict with each other in actual play anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well first of all what if someone runs a WoD/CoD crossover game using Requiem PCs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T20:09:24-08:00","id":1012950,"title":"","content":"Did you once post here under a different name? Your questions are really familiar.<br /> <br /> Someone doing that and, for whatever reason, not using the translation guides, is asking to have a lot of work to do.<br /> <br /> That said, people have a really skewed version of what's balanced or not and no one answer would past the individual table it's being played at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T20:22:08-08:00","id":1012956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008163-making-discplines-more-useful-in-combat?p=1012945#post1012945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well first of all what if someone runs a WoD/CoD crossover game using Requiem PCs?</div> </div> </div> </div>Then any imbalance issues they might run into are not the fault of the individual settings they are trying to mash together. As with any crossover, the writer (or in this case, the Storyteller) has to do the work to smooth over the parts where the settings don't quite fit together perfectly. The translation guides are a tool to help STs who want to blend elements of the two settings, but one setting shouldn't be constrained by the other just in case someone, somewhere, gets it in their head that they want to do a mashup.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T23:41:05-08:00","id":1013034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008163-making-discplines-more-useful-in-combat?p=1012858#post1012858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh one last question, does 2nd edition Requiem Vampires able to stand a chance against VtM vampires? If not then this is why their powers need a little more beefing up to match them.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said, definetely yes and, a requiem built to fight, is even more powerful compared to a masquerade built to fight (translating masquerade character into requiem system).<br /> You should provide us some example of disciplines that you don't find so useful in combat compared with the masquerade counterpart so we could discuss on something concrete.<br /> The 3 physical disciplines are on the side of requiem (hard to say for celerity only because the requiem system don't allow for multiple actions at all). The other discipline are on the side of requiem too according to me. Just some example:<br /> <br /> Nightmare 2 vs presence 2 (Dread Gaze): in requiem, if you win the contested roll (1 success), the targhet escapes . In masquerade you need to perform multiple roll in order to reach the same effect.<br /> <br /> Majesty 3 is more effective than presence 3.<br /> <br /> Majesty 4 even have not a masquerade counterpart at all.<br /> <br /> Majesty 3-4 allow you to force an enemy to fight by your side while masquerade presence doesen't.<br /> <br /> Presence 7 allow you to rise a riot in a crowd and you can achieve the same effect with just animalism 4 in requiem.<br /> <br /> Requiem Protean is far more powerful in combat than masquerade version.<br /> <br /> Obfuscate 3 is far more effective in requiem than in masquerade. In requiem you can disappear and even interact (fight or talk) with an enemy without being seen by the others and, with the same power, you can subtract another person from the perception (both enemy or ally).<br /> <br /> Requiem dominate 1 allow you to give 4 words command, masquerade domination 1 just 1 word and not in fight. You can give commands also during a fight in requiem while in masquerade they have effect just for one single turn. Furthemore dominate in requiem, allow you to give commands that with the masquerade version they wouldn't never been acomplished unless you achieve an exceptional success in the roll.<br /> <br /> ...and so on.... Provide me some example to understand your point of view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 12-06-2016, 06:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T04:21:17-08:00","id":1013095,"title":"","content":"Requium vampires are better combat monsters than Masquerade vampires. They also progress faster and neonates have a much higher ceiling since their &quot;blood potency&quot; isn't set at birth.<br /> <br /> As for doing shadow tentacles with Khaibit. Get a chain, do the shadow covering devotion and the create shadow patch devotion. Load up on Vigor and Strength.<br /> <br /> Use it on a chain, which you can now telekinetically control. You may also lift and throw cars with it.<br /> <br /> Not enough? Combine with the item creation rules in cofd core to get a 4L (Grapple) chain. Now you can also rip through cars like butter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T12:09:22-08:00","id":1013307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008163-making-discplines-more-useful-in-combat?p=1012950#post1012950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you once post here under a different name? Your questions are really familiar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for pointing this out. Yeah, Veindark appears to be a dummy account for a previously banned user.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}